 34MG c  Beam={+34}Mg at 51.1 MeV/nucleon, target=liquid hydrogen. Proton-proton
 34MG2c  inelastic scattering in inverse kinematics used to determine           
 34MG3c  deformation length and |b{-2} for first 2+ state                       
 34MG c  {+34}Mg produced by fragmentation of 63 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam with  
 34MG2c  {+181}Ta and enriched {+64}Ni target foils of 150 |mm and 200 |mm      
 34MG3c  thicknesses, respectively at RFQ-RILAC-CSM-RRC accelerator at RIKEN    
 34MG4c  facility. The fragments were separated and identified by RIPS fragment 
 34MG5c  separator optimized for A/Z=3 reaction products. Particle              
 34MG6c  identification was made from measurements of magnetic rigidity (B|r),  
 34MG7c  time-of-flight (tof), and energy loss (|DE-E). The secondary beam of   
 34MG8c  {+34}Mg at 51.1 MeV/nucleon hit a liquid hydrogen target (CRYPTA). The 
 34MG9c  scattered particles were analyzed by the TOMBEE spectrometer consisting
 34MGAc  of a superconducting triplet quadrupole, plastic scintillator, and a   
 34MGBc  |DE-E telescope of a silicon detector and a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured 
 34MGCc  E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin using DALI2 array of 160 NaI(Tl) detectors         
 34MGDc  surrounding the hydrogen target. In order to apply Doppler correction  
 34MGEc  to the measured |g-ray energies, angles of the |g rays were measured   
 34MGFc  relative to the trajectories of the scattered particles. The scattering
 34MGGc  angles were measured using two parallel-plate avalanche counters (PPAC)
 34MGHc  upstream and one PPAC detector downstream from the {+1}H target.       
 34MGIc  Deduced deformation lengths and |b{-2} deformation parameter from the  
 34MGJc  analysis of measured angle-integrated cross section by coupled-channel 
 34MGKc  calculations with the ECIS97 computer code, and WP09 global potential. 
 34MGLc  Comparison with shell-model (SDPF-M) calculations, and with previous   
 34MGMc  experimental results                                                   
 34MG c  2006EL03: a 94-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was transported to a   
 34MG2c  {+181}Ta primary target. Tge secondary beams of 30Na, 31Na, {+33}Mg,   
 34MG3c  and {+34}Mg were separated by the RIPS fragment separator and bombarded
 34MG4c  a liquid hydrogen target at a mean energy of 50 MeV/nucleon. The       
 34MG5c  reaction products were detected and identified by a parallel-plate     
 34MG6c  avalanche counter (PPAC) and a silicon detector telescope. The         
 34MG7c  deexciting |g rays emitted by the inelastically scattered nuclei were  
 34MG8c  detected by the DALI2 setup consisting of 146 NaI(Tl) detectors.       
 34MG9c  Deduced mass deformation and neutron deformation parameters.           
